<p>I'm embarrassed to say this did not even trip my radar while critting. But now that you bring it up, I can definitely see the objection.</p>
<p>I have a notion which would provide a fairly clean workaround. (Though it's up to rounder and dog if they are interested in using this or some other idea here &#8212; the article as-is is clearly succeeding!)</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">WHAT&nbsp;IF</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">what&nbsp;if&nbsp;the&nbsp;cult&nbsp;/&nbsp;team&nbsp;interprets&nbsp;'youth'&nbsp;very&nbsp;broadly?</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>In the current &quot;Test 8&quot;, the &quot;Resources&quot; box is redacted, implying they went out an got an actual child. If instead, that box said &quot;Researcher XXX, the youngest member of the containment team&quot;, this could theoretically still qualify as a <em>youth</em>. Or at least, the most youthful person who was immediately available to the team.</p>
<p>Now, I'd interpreted Tests 6 and 7 to mean the swine god was displeased with the offering given to it in Test 6, that is, an already-deceased person. It retaliated against this insult by being exceptionally cruel to the person in Test 7, by making them suffer for hours before they died.</p>
<p>Test 9 is already pretty horrific &#8212; <strong>450 kilograms</strong> is just under 1000 pounds of coal. Being manually shoveled by two people. That's a hellacious amount of shoveling. And after and/or during all that shoveling, one of the researchers is burned to death while the other is severely injured.</p>
<p>So if the change were made, one could easily interpret the nastiness of Test 9 as the swine god's retaliation for being given <em>merely</em> a somewhat youthful researcher rather than the actual child it demanded in Test 8.</p>
</div>
</div>
